<item><title>Algeria’s parallel market asks 27 700 dinars for 100 euros</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algeria-s-parallel-market-asks-27-700-dinars-for-100-euros-a809b8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algeria-s-parallel-market-asks-27-700-dinars-for-100-euros-a809b8/</guid><category>Algeria</category><description>Currency dealers offered 27 450 dinars to buy 100 euros on Tuesday, against the central bank’s official rate of 150,49 dinars per euro.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:17:13 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algeria-s-parallel-market-asks-27-700-dinars-for-100-euros-a809b8/share.jpg" length="40578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algeria-s-parallel-market-asks-27-700-dinars-for-100-euros-a809b8/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
